  "name": "Email document intake: OCR, classify, file to Drive, and index every attachment",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "e43c96b4-33f9-486a-b3aa-9a76978e8900",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -512,
        768
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 752,
        "height": 1664,
        "content": "# Email document intake: complete instructions\n\n\n**Community node.** This template uses the pdfRest API Toolkit community node (@pdfrest/n8n-nodes-pdfrest), so it runs on self-hosted n8n only. Install it under Settings > Community Nodes before importing.\n\n### Who it's for\n\nTeams whose inbox is a document intake channel: accounts payable, legal ops, property management, anyone who receives invoices, contracts, and signed forms by email and files them by hand.\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow monitors Gmail for incoming messages, splits each attachment into its own item, and standardizes the binary data for processing. \n\nIt checks PDF metadata, applies OCR when needed, converts the document to markdown, and uses an AI-powered Information Extractor (Anthropic Claude shown; any chat model works) to classify the document. \n\nBased on the classification, it files the attachment into the correct Google Drive folder, appends an index row in Google Sheets, and sends a Slack notification.\n\n\n\n## Attachment preparation\n\nSplits the email into one item per attachment, normalizes the binary field, and branches PDF attachments for additional inspection.\n\n\n---\n\n## PDF metadata check\n\npdfRest Query PDF Info returns page count and whether the file is image-only (a scan with no text layer) as JSON. Merge PDF Data rejoins that JSON with the item that still carries the PDF binary.\n\n---\n\n## OCR decision path\n\nImage-only scans go through pdfRest OCR and get a searchable text layer. Born-digital PDFs skip it. Each item is marked with whether OCR was applied.\n\n---\n\n## Extract and classify\n\npdfRest converts the PDF to Markdown (JSON output). The Information Extractor reads the first 12,000 characters and returns documentType, counterparty, and documentDate. Merge for Filing reattaches the PDF binary for upload.\n\n---\n\n## Choose filing destination\n\nRoutes the classified document type and sets the target folder ID plus normalized document type for each filing category.\n\n---\n\n## Upload filed document\n\nUploads the processed attachment to the selected Google Drive folder.\n\n---\n\n## Index and notify\n\nRecords the uploaded document in Google Sheets and sends a Slack notification when indexing is complete.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
