    {
      "id": "48a43196-e28c-402e-a4bc-9cdc4ddf1e91",
      "name": "Setup checklist",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        608,
        608
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 672,
        "height": 592,
        "content": "\n### Setup steps\n\n\n- Connect and authorize the Gmail trigger for the mailbox or label that receives document intake emails.\n\n- Configure the folder IDs, index Sheet ID, Slack channel ID (right-click the channel in Slack > View channel details), and OCR languages in the Set Folder and Index IDs node.\n\n- Add a pdfRest API credential (API key from pdfrest.com) for the three pdfRest nodes and confirm the expected binary property is `data`.\n\n- Connect an Anthropic credential to the Anthropic Chat Model subnode (or swap in OpenAI, Gemini, or a local model) and verify the Document Type Classifier output matches the Route by Document Type switch rules.\n\n- Authorize Google Drive and Google Sheets credentials, then select the destination Drive folders and the spreadsheet used as the document index.\n\n- Authorize Slack credentials and configure the target channel or user for completion notifications.\n\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "edf0ab73-dfa5-4eed-91bd-14395fba69c2",
      "name": "Customization guide",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2544,
        592
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 672,
        "height": 592,
        "content": "### Customization\n\nYou can adjust the document categories, folder mappings, classification prompt/schema, index columns, and Slack message content to match your filing taxonomy.\n\nTo add a document type: add it to the attribute description in Document Type Classifier, add a rule in Route by Document Type, add a Prepare node for it, and a folder ID in Set Folder and Index IDs.\n\nFor records retention, add pdfRest's Convert \u00b7 PDF to PDF/A (Archival) after Apply OCR to PDF.\n\nSwap Slack for Microsoft Teams or email, or narrow the Gmail filter to a label for a single-purpose inbox."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
